{title: Come To The Table}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: G}
{tempo: 129}

Verse 1
[D]Come to the table,
[A]There is [Bm]room for all.
[A]The [D]bread is served,
[A]The wine [A]is [Bm]poured.
[D]Behold our Savior
[A]Hear His [Bm7]loving [G]call,
[A]He shows The Way,
[A]He is The [Bm]Door.

Chorus
[E]We [G]are invited [D]now
So let [F#]us enter [Bm]in.
[A]No [G]one [A]denied,
None [D]turned [D7]away.
[G]The Savior calls [D]to us
So [F#]let the feast begin,
[G]Enter the everlasting [D]day.

Verse 2
[Bm7]Come [A]to [D]the [A]table,
leave your [Bm]past behind,
[A7]Lay [D]all your cares [A]before His [Bm]throne.
[D]Abundant mercy,
[A]His [Bm7]forgiveness [G]find,
[D]Rejoice in [A]your eternal [Bm]home!
[E](Repeat chorus)
[Em7]We [G]are invited [D]now
So [F#]let us enter [Bm]in.
[G]No one denied,
[D]None turned [D7]away.
[G]The Savior calls [D]to us
So [F#]let the feast [Bm]begin,
[G]Enter the everlasting [D]day.
[A#](Raise key)

Verse 3
[D#]Come [D#]to the table,
Bring your neighbors, too.
[D#]Plead with them all to come inside.
[D#]Tell of the [A#]One
Who makes each [Cm]heart brand new,
[D#]In whom our [A#]souls are [Cm]satisfied!
[F](Repeat chorus 2 times)
[G#]We are invited now
So [G]let us enter [Cm]in.
[G#]No one denied,
[A#]None turned away.
[D#7]The [G#]Savior calls to us
So [D#]let [G]the feast [Cm7]begin,
[G#]Enter the everlasting [A#]day.

Ending
[Emaj7]Enter [E]the everlasting day.
